WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.700
One matched pilot pair, recorded one run
after the other on the same physical arm.

2
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:14.800
Can a Python program help Fable land
the film carton closer to the target?

3
00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:22.600
Both runs get front and wrist camera views
and readings of the five arm joints.

4
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:30.500
Both choose the next joint angles. Only
the right run can also write and run Python.

5
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.800
Place the pink-banded Fuji within 15 mm
of an unmarked point on the tray.

6
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:47.100
Align the long edge within 15° of the arm’s
forward axis. Release and stay clear for 3 s.

7
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:59.100
While the arm is parked, Python returns
a grid on the first camera image.

8
00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:19.150
On the right, Python prints five angles
for the arm joints.

9
00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:27.100
The right arm reaches. It reports its
first completed move at 2:24.

10
00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:28.800
The right gripper closes on the carton.

11
00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:02.100
The right arm lifts the carton clear
of the bench.

12
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:15.600
It carries the carton over the tray.

13
00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:31.800
The right gripper lowers the carton
onto the tray, then opens.

14
00:04:49.075 --> 00:04:57.000
The right run ends at 4:49.
The left arm’s first move ends at 4:50.

15
00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:21.400
The left gripper closes on its carton
and lifts it.

16
00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:59.600
The left arm carries the carton
toward the same target.

17
00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:21.100
The left gripper opens and lifts clear.
The carton stays on the tray.

18
00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:29.900
Center errors were 3.1 mm without Python
and 4.5 mm with it. Both placements passed.
